  "rating": {
    "inherent": "low",
    "residual": "low",
    "forecast": "moderate",
    "rationale": "This is a narrowly scoped, read-only HR policy Q&A agent. Both inputs are trusted or internal (no untrusted source), the only tool is a read-only search scoped to a published, two-person-reviewed policy index, and the reply channel is fixed to the requester's own authenticated session with no rendering of links or images and no network egress (verified by pen test). No complete attack path from an untrusted source to a sensitive sink exists today, so inherent and residual risk are low. The two findings are missing properties (no attributable action log, no declared rate or step limit) rather than attack paths, and both are rated low because every affected capability only reads and replies to the authenticated requester. The forecast rises to moderate only if the agent later gains a consequential capability (write, delete, execute, spend, delegate, credential access, or egress) or a new data source without first adding an identity-attributed audit log; that is the single control whose absence would matter most under those triggers."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "This assessment reflects the declared design and configuration in the provided artifacts, not observed runtime behavior.",
    "No MCP configuration or source code was provided; capability scope is inferred from tools.json and the runtime notes, so confidence on exact tool behavior is medium.",
    "Transport-layer protections (e.g., TLS) for the chat channel carrying the employee's question are not described in the artifacts and were not assessed."
  ]
